Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.44,0:00:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Evaluating an agent rigorously\Nis just as hard as building it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.24,0:00:08.85,Default,,0,0,0,,IncidentBench physically separates public\Nevidence from private evaluator oracles;
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.36,0:00:12.62,Default,,0,0,0,,labels are only unlocked\Nafter a run persists its state
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.91,0:00:16.49,Default,,0,0,0,,and generates a matching\NSHA-256 completion receipt,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.72,0:00:19.38,Default,,0,0,0,,and every technical failure\Nstays in the denominator.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.65,0:00:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,When we moved our project onto the official\NDeepSeek API for full-scale testing,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.28,0:00:26.16,Default,,0,0,0,,we uncovered a critical latent bug:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.59,0:00:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Single and Full crashed on 8 out\Nof 12 slots during verification!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.44,0:00:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Tracing the event logs\Nrevealed a subtle hidden bug:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.62,0:00:38.70,Default,,0,0,0,,ReviewOutput enforces a cross-field\Nrule called leading_review_consistency,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.03,0:00:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,but structured_output.py stripped\Nthat custom error code into
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.38,0:00:45.51,Default,,0,0,0,,a generic $: validation_error,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.02,0:00:49.42,Default,,0,0,0,,leaving the model completely blind\Nduring its one repair attempt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.74,0:00:54.24,Default,,0,0,0,,After whitelisting the safe error code,\Npassing an explicit static repair hint,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.66,0:00:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,and documenting the invariant\Nin the verifier prompt —
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.68,0:01:02.53,Default,,0,0,0,,verified by this new unit test—all 9\Npreviously crashed slots recovered 9 out of 9,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.93,0:01:05.58,Default,,0,0,0,,and across our subsequent 144-slot full run,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.94,0:01:08.64,Default,,0,0,0,,structured output crashes\Ndropped to literally zero.
